\tag{decision}
\tag{area:rt}
\tag{status:superseded}

\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{\code{Interface/} exports, and \code{Theory/} may use, exactly:}
  \ul{
    \li{\strong{Shapes, transparently}: the objects and morphisms of Δ, Δ₊, Ω_p, Ω, Θ^aug_fc, Θ_n, Δ×Δ, □, \code{Tw(θ)} are exported as \em{transparent} inductive types with \code{DecidableEq} and computable composition (→ \ref{dec-tl-0010}): rows of block sizes for \code{Θ^aug_fc}, monotone \code{Fin} maps for Δ, nested lists for Ω_p and Θ_n, and so on. What is sealed is their \code{Category} structure in the sense of \ref{dec-rt-0010} (with generating morphisms, inert/active factorization, degrees, Segal cores, labelled variants as API) and the bridge lemma identifying the transparent hom-types with the sealed ones. This is the one deliberate exposure of computation past the seal: a pasting proof is a tree-map equality decided on finite data (→ \ref{dec-tl-0009}), not a fact about how a categorical notion unfolds, so \ref{dec-ch-0001} is not violated; the linter's \code{decide} ban (→ \ref{dec-tl-0006}) exempts these types.}
    \li{\strong{Spaces}: \code{Space} (Kan complexes), maps, homotopy, homotopy equivalence, \code{π₀}, contractibility, fibrations and fibre products, mapping spaces — sealed.}
    \li{\strong{Root}: \code{VDC∞}, maps, \code{Vert}, \code{Hor}, \code{hP}, DK-equivalence, fibrant, fibrant replacement (existence), \code{Map}.}
    \li{\strong{Constructions}: \code{N} (discrete embedding), walking structures, \code{Monad}, \code{Bimodule}, \code{Mod}, \code{Mat Set}, \code{Category}, \code{Cat}, the self-hosting theorem.}
    \li{\strong{Closure and rectification} (→ \ref{dec-ch-0013}), as theorems: \code{Mat Set} is fibrant (trivially); \code{Mod} preserves fibrancy; slices, functor objects (mapping Segal categories), and fibre products along fibrations preserve fibrancy; exponentials of fibrant objects by cofibrant ones are fibrant; the pushout-product and Reedy lemmas needed to prove such statements in \code{Theory/}; DK-invariance of \code{Mod}, \code{Vert}, \code{Hor}, \code{hP}; rectification: for a strict (Segal, not necessarily fibrant) \code{P}, strict maps \code{N W → P} composed with \code{P → RP} hit every component of \code{Map(N W, P)} (Dwyer–Kan/Bergner rigidification in the case \code{P = Mat Kan}, → \ref{dec-sp-0004}). Later interface versions add the same package for \code{Mat Kan}, \code{Span}, and limits.}
    \li{\strong{Nothing else.} No \code{SSet}, no \code{SimplexCategory}, no Mathlib \code{Functor}.}
  }
  \p{Extension policy, two tiers:}
  \ul{
    \li{\strong{Constants} (new sealed data or new shapes) are frozen-tier: a superseding decision.}
    \li{\strong{Lemmas} statable in interface vocabulary and provable in \code{Root/} are provisional-tier: an agent may add them by PR without a decision, subject to the statement-hygiene check (3). This is expected to be the dominant kind of change after \ref{ms-0003}, and making it cheap is what keeps the seal from making the human the bottleneck.}
  }
  \p{Mechanism:}
  \ol{
    \li{Data whose definitional equations are never needed in \code{Theory/} are \code{opaque} constants with their kernel implementation as the inhabitation witness.}
    \li{Data whose equations \em{are} needed as API are \code{@[irreducible]} definitions with equation lemmas \code{foo_def} that are \code{private} to \code{Root/}; the exported API consists of theorems proved in \code{Root/} using those lemmas.}
    \li{Every exported theorem is stated purely in interface vocabulary. A CI grep enforces that \code{Interface/} mentions no kernel or Mathlib category-theory names in statements.}
    \li{The \strong{swap test} (→ \ref{dec-tl-0006}): a second \code{Interface-Stub/} in which every constant is a bodiless \code{axiom} with the same statement; \code{Theory/} must build against it.}
    \li{A build variant that uses the stub instead of the kernel for speed; the kernel build is the consistency witness and runs nightly.}
  }
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{\code{opaque} is the hard seal; \code{@[irreducible]} + private equations is the soft seal that still allows API lemmas to be proved once; the swap test is the proof that no leak exists, and it is what "axiom wlog" (→ \ref{dec-ch-0012}) means operationally.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen; the interface \em{list} is frozen at \ref{ms-0003} ("Interface v1") and extended only by superseding decisions.}
}
